---

<section class="py-14 lg:py-20 bg-lavender reveal">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">

      <!-- Photo -->
      <div class="flex justify-center lg:justify-start">
        <img src="/formal.png" alt="Eric" class="w-56 h-56 lg:w-72 lg:h-72 rounded-xl object-cover border-3 border-ink shadow-offset-md" />
      </div>

      <!-- Text -->
      <div>
        <p class="text-ink text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">About Eric</p>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-extrabold text-ink tracking-tight mb-5">
          I've spent 4 years teaching <i>just</i> this one test.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-ink/80 font-semibold leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Back in 2021, I scored a perfect 800 on the SAT Math both times I took it.
            My goal as a tutor is to help other students do the same.
          </p>
          <p>
            I recently graduated from the University of Virginia, majoring in Computer Science
            and Economics with a minor in Math. Along the way, I've taught hundreds of students directly
            and become the <b>most-viewed SAT math creator on the internet.</b>
          </p>
          <p>
            As a lifelong student, I know the pitfalls of education firsthand, and I've become
            obsessed with the science behind how we actually learn. Most test prep is dry, outdated,
            and focused more on brute-forcing problems than truly understanding them.
            I'm here to change that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/masterclass"
          class="inline-block mt-7 bg-electric text-ink font-black px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full border-2 border-ink shadow-offset-sm hover:shadow-none hover:translate-x-[3px] hover:translate-y-[3px] transition-all duration-200 text-base tracking-wide"
        >
          Work with me →
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
